# Daily Stargazing Plan TODO adapter

Apply this rule only while the shared `execute-plan-todo` skill is active.

## Plans and branches

- Phase plans live under `.cursor/plans/Phase*.plan.md` and use YAML frontmatter `todos:` entries with `id`, `content`, and `status`.
- Use branch names in the form `<type>/phase<N.N...>-<todo-name>`.
- Default to the latest `main` after the previous dependency is complete and merged.
- A downstream TODO may inherit an unmerged predecessor branch only when the plan or user explicitly authorizes stacked development. Record the predecessor branch in the report.

## Verification

- This is a Python project; run relevant tests with `python -m pytest <test-path>`.
- Run broader `python -m pytest` only when the TODO scope or acceptance criteria require it.
- Preserve local environment and output artifacts that are outside the TODO scope.

## Human gate and completion

- A TODO requires human approval when `[需人工验收]` appears in its `content` or corresponding section title.
- Before approval, the implementation commit is allowed when authorized, but plan completion, final report, push, merge request, and merge are blocked.
- After approval, change the canonical YAML `status` to `complete`; do not use Markdown checkboxes as the source of truth.
- Reports live at `docs/reports/Phase<N.N...>-<todo-name>-report.md`.
- Use Conventional Commits in the form `<type>(<scope>): p<N.N>-<description>` when compatible with recent repository history.
- Publish through a GitLab merge request and preserve required checks and branch protection.
- Human merge and Issue closure approval remain mandatory. Editorial publication still requires separate explicit authorization.
